      "writtenOn": "2022-07-18T09:56:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For SAFER as it\u0027s \"only\" used for Message Authentication Code (MAC) we only need the encrypt function, if we want to follow completely the spec we might just implement one but for a MAC I think we can ignore that and do something custom.\n\nFor ECDH doing `openssl ecparam -list_curves` seems to list me the two curves that we want `prime192v1` for P192 and `prime256v1` for P256.\nAnd they seems available in Rust https://docs.rs/openssl/latest/openssl/nid/struct.Nid.html#associatedconstant.X9_62_PRIME192V1",
      "parentUuid": "fb3c5c31_e562e170",
      "revId": "47ffe90d2a01950324c6b531755c5e95abb353c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
